extent for typed immutable evidence and neutral references: typed Definition/Observation/Verdict admission, immutable digest-backed evidence objects, CAS operational pointers after durable writes, neutral references, and integration with the existing verdict evaluator without creating new policy or absorbing sibling scopes.\",\"implementation_unknowns\":[\"Exact repository locations and current interfaces for the evidence_learning port/local adapter, shared neutral Ref values, composition/evidence_profile.py, and existing evaluate_verdict bridge are not established by the packet.\",\"The concrete durable-write mechanism, fsync/install ordering, CAS pointer implementation, and crash-before/crash-after fixture approach require engineering discovery against the codebase.\",\"The exact executable fixture commands, inputs, expected outputs, evidence schema, and negative-control mutation points must be pinned before implementation as the packet requires.\",\"The migration details for creating version-1 immutable external objects and validating typed links need implementation-level mapping to the existing persistence model.\"],\"independent_decision_centers\":[],\"material_risks\":[\"Required predecessor completion for WO-220101/S0 is a stated dependency, and the supplied packet does not include the exact independently verified predecessor proof receipts it requires.\",\"Release/work-management admission is expressly separate and not granted by the packet; attempting implementation without those gates would violate the packet\\u2019s own custody and authority constraints.\",\"Incorrect handling of role, authority, revision, or digest validation could allow unauthorized PASS verdicts, which is the central safety property of the work.\",\"Crash-ordering and durable-write behavior may be platform-sensitive and must be tested with discriminating fixtures rather than inferred from local success.\",\"Migration/rollback errors could leave incompatible schemas, stale pointers, or 